### Define Shrinking Tests in PHP

Source: https://eris.readthedocs.io/en/latest/shrinking.html

Demonstrates how to use Eris generators and test traits to define properties that trigger shrinking upon failure.

```php
<?php
use Eris\Generator;
use Eris\TestTrait;

class ShrinkingTest extends \PHPUnit_Framework_TestCase
{
    use TestTrait;

    public function testShrinkingAString()
    {
        $this->forAll(
                Generator\string()
            )
            ->then(function ($string) {
                var_dump($string);
                $this->assertNotContains('B', $string);
            });
    }

    public function testShrinkingRespectsAntecedents()
    {
        $this->forAll(
                Generator\choose(0, 20)
            )
            ->when(function ($number) {
                return $number > 10;
            })
            ->then(function ($number) {
                $this->assertTrue($number % 29 == 0, "The number $number is not multiple of 29");
            });
    }
}
```

--------------------------------

### Reproduce a test failure with a specific seed

Source: https://eris.readthedocs.io/en/latest/reproducibility.html

Use the ERIS_SEED environment variable to force the generator to use a specific seed, ensuring the same random inputs are selected for a test.

```bash
ERIS_SEED=1458646953837419 vendor/bin/phpunit --filter AlwaysFailsTest::testFailsNoMatterWhatIsTheInput
```

```bash
$ ERIS_SEED=1458646953837419 vendor/bin/phpunit --filter AlwaysFailsTest::testFailsNoMatterWhatIsTheInput
```

--------------------------------

### Configure Eris test limits in PHP

Source: https://eris.readthedocs.io/en/latest/limits.html

Demonstrates using @eris-repeat and @eris-duration annotations alongside the limitTo() method to control test execution.

```php
<?php
use Eris\Generator;
use Eris\TestTrait;

class LimitToTest extends PHPUnit_Framework_TestCase
{
    use TestTrait;

    /**
     * @eris-repeat 5
     */
    public function testNumberOfIterationsCanBeConfigured()
    {
        $this->forAll(
                Generator\int()
            )
            ->then(function ($value) {
                $this->assertInternalType('integer', $value);
            });
    }

    /*
     * future feature
    public function testTimeIntervalToRunForCanBeConfiguredButItNeedsToProduceAtLeastHalfOfTheIterationsByDefault()
    {
        $this->minimum(10)
             ->limitTo(new DateInterval("PT2S"))
             ->forAll(
                Generator\int()
            )
            ->then(function($value) {
                usleep(100 * 1000);
                $this->assertTrue(true);
            });
    }
     */

    public function testTimeIntervalToRunForCanBeConfiguredAndAVeryLowNumberOfIterationsCanBeIgnored()
    {
        $this
            ->minimumEvaluationRatio(0)
            ->limitTo(new DateInterval('PT2S'))
            ->forAll(
                Generator\int()
            )
            ->then(function ($value) {
                usleep(100 * 1000);
                $this->assertTrue(true);
            });
    }

    /**
     * @eris-ratio 0
     * @eris-duration PT2S
     */
    public function testTimeIntervalToRunForCanBeConfiguredAndAVeryLowNumberOfIterationsCanBeIgnoredFromAnnotation()
    {
        $this->forAll(
                Generator\int()
            )
            ->then(function ($value) {
                usleep(100 * 1000);
                $this->assertTrue(true);
            });
    }
}
```

--------------------------------

### Run Eris example tests

Source: https://eris.readthedocs.io/en/latest/installation.html

Execute the provided example tests using the PHPUnit binary located in the vendor directory.

```bash
vendor/bin/phpunit vendor/giorgiosironi/eris/examples
```

### Listeners

Source: https://eris.readthedocs.io/en/latest/listeners.html

Eris allows the use of Listeners to monitor events during a test run. Listeners should implement the Eris\Listener interface and are encouraged to extend the Eris\EmptyListener base class to provide default implementations for unused event methods. By default, Eris performs 100 iterations for each property verification, with each iteration using a unique set of generated values.

