### Configure Fuzzing Target with Max Input Length

Source: https://context7.com/nikic/php-fuzzer/llms.txt

Sets the fuzzing target and limits the maximum length of generated inputs using `Config::setMaxLen()`. This example targets a custom parser and limits inputs to 1KB, improving performance by focusing on shorter, potentially bug-revealing inputs.

```php
<?php // target.php

/** @var PhpFuzzer\Config $config */

require 'vendor/autoload.php';

$parser = new MyParser();

$config->setTarget(function(string $input) use ($parser) {
    $parser->parse($input);
});

// Limit inputs to 1KB - good for most parsing targets
$config->setMaxLen(1024);
```

--------------------------------

### Start Fuzzing with Initial Corpus

Source: https://github.com/nikic/php-fuzzer/blob/master/README.md

Initiates the fuzzing process for a target PHP script using an initial corpus of input files. The corpus directory should contain one input file per entry.

```shell
php-fuzzer fuzz target.php corpus/
```

--------------------------------

### Define Target Function for PHP-Fuzzer

Source: https://github.com/nikic/php-fuzzer/blob/master/README.md

This PHP code snippet demonstrates how to define a target function for the PHP-Fuzzer. It sets up the parser and configures the fuzzer to use the parser's `parseSourceFile` method with a given input string. It also shows optional configurations for maximum input length and adding a dictionary for improved fuzzing.

```php
<?php // target.php

/** @var PhpFuzzer\Config $config */

require 'path/to/tolerant-php-parser/vendor/autoload.php';

// Required: The target accepts a single input string and runs it through the tested
//           library. The target is allowed to throw normal Exceptions (which are ignored),
//           but Error exceptions are considered as a found bug.
$parser = new Microsoft\PhpParser\Parser();
$config->setTarget(function(string $input) use($parser) {
    $parser->parseSourceFile($input);
});

// Optional: Many targets don't exhibit bugs on large inputs that can't also be
//           produced with small inputs. Limiting the length may improve performance.
$config->setMaxLen(1024);
// Optional: A dictionary can be used to provide useful fragments to the fuzzer,
//           such as language keywords. This is particularly important if these
//           cannot be easily discovered by the fuzzer, because they are handled
//           by a non-instrumented PHP extension function such as token_get_all().
$config->addDictionary('example/php.dict');

```

--------------------------------

### Complete PHP Fuzzer Workflow Example

Source: https://context7.com/nikic/php-fuzzer/llms.txt

This bash script outlines a complete workflow for using PHP Fuzzer. It covers creating an initial corpus, starting a fuzzing session, minimizing any found crashes, debugging them with `run-single`, generating coverage reports, and resuming fuzzing.

```bash
# 1. Create initial corpus from existing test cases
mkdir -p corpus
cp tests/fixtures/*.txt corpus/

# 2. Start fuzzing session
php-fuzzer fuzz target.php corpus/
# Press Ctrl+C to stop

# 3. If crashes are found, minimize them
php-fuzzer minimize-crash target.php crash-abc123.txt

# 4. Debug the minimized crash
php-fuzzer run-single target.php minimized-def456.txt

# 5. Generate coverage report to find gaps
php-fuzzer report-coverage target.php corpus/ coverage/

# 6. Resume fuzzing later (corpus state is preserved)
php-fuzzer fuzz target.php corpus/
```

--------------------------------

### Minimize Crash Input with PHP Fuzzer CLI

Source: https://context7.com/nikic/php-fuzzer/llms.txt

The `minimize-crash` command reduces a crashing input file to its smallest possible size while ensuring it still triggers the same crash. This is crucial for efficient debugging. It takes the target script and the crash file as arguments and outputs successively smaller minimized files.

```bash
# Minimize a crash file
php-fuzzer minimize-crash target.php crash-abc123.txt

# Output produces successively smaller files:
# CRASH with length 512 in minimized-def456.txt!
# CRASH with length 256 in minimized-ghi789.txt!
# CRASH with length 64 in minimized-jkl012.txt!

# Limit minimization runs
php-fuzzer --max-runs=50000 minimize-crash target.php crash-abc123.txt
```

